[124.06696, "o", "197:to a temperature greater than its melting point. One can\r\n304:elevated to a temperature greater than the melting point\r\n306:temperature is 183°C. This temperature must be exceeded by approximately 20°C to ensure quality reflow.\r\n642:as not to exceed the 2OC/sec rate. When operating at\r\n868:exceed the gas flow temperature. This is useful when\r\n1056:Operating at a conveyor speed greater than the calculated\r\n1067:speed defined below must be greater than the minimum\r\n1405:where the product temperature is greater than 150°C,\r\n1454:exceeds 20% capacity, resulting in lamp life in excess of\r\n1502:operate at a level greater than their setpoint. The lamp\r\n1620:has lateral warpage of greater than this amount, the\r\n"]
